    "successor_implication": "Correctly partially applies the dispatcher budget before passing it to consumerStep, and supplies the new explicit budget at eight remaining fixture placement/dispatch/render call sites. No production/scientific source or operator configuration changes from47750. The earlier call defect is resolved at actual affected-component compilation and three synthetic regression scope.",
    "numerical_source": "No numerical algorithm, optimizer/training recipe, canonical matrix/projection, seeds, data/split, evaluation/reference, convergence floor, qualification/admission or cohort comparison implementation is among the12 changed files. Those source-owned policies remain among605 exact matches. Resource plumbing can change time/resource failure behavior, so actual successful unchanged-budget completion must still be measured.",
    "resource_change": "Adds numericalWorkload ComponentBudget through ClusterResources/Dhall, mounted BootConfig, bootstrap/coordinator, Workload dispatch/placement and all four numerical Job kinds. resourceLines explicitly renders requests/limits instead of accidental supporting LimitRange inheritance. Default request1CPU/2Gi, limit2CPU/4Gi; Mac request250m/1Gi, limit1CPU/1536Mi; replicas1. Positive quantities/request<=limit and replicas1 are validated; resource-envelope component checks include per-node request/memory-limit fit. Apple Cluster launches still forward host commands.",
    "resource_limitations": "Per-component arithmetic is not simultaneous pod bin-packing or live memory/time fit. replicas1 does not prove global serialization of independently launched Jobs. Linux VM/container limits do not constrain host Metal/ARS CPU/heap; a native supervised budget remains separately necessary. No criterion, work allocation, wall deadline or failure is waived.",
    "source_coverage": "Algorithm1 source digest covers app/gen/src/test and the two Cabal project files. Root operator Dhall is outside617 and is independently pinned here.",
